 works as expected. Code looks good to me.\r\n\r\nSome changes need to be made before this can be merged though:\r\n\r\n- The **Close Curve** button in the Path2D should toggle the Curve2D resource's **Closed** property instead of creating a new point at the first point's position. Check `path_3d_editor_plugin.cpp` as for how it implements that.\r\n- The beginning and end curve points should be colorized to match the 3D editor:\r\n\r\nNon-closed curve (green = first point, red = last point):\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9351933d-bff3-48ad-b53c-6584c399af92)\r\n\r\nClosed curve (yellow = first point):\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f942bf9d-1955-4a7d-8914-dee10984e560)\r\n\r\nYou can find the exact colors used for those [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/931820d33cbc38328e4014d65dd62c359b5116fc/editor/plugins/path_3d_editor_plugin.cpp#L311-L313).","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105635#pullrequestreview-2788198790","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105635","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105635#pullrequestreview-2788198790"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105635"}},"submitted_at":"2025-04-23T17:31:26Z","commit_id":null}]